# S-022 QUIRK Q-5: the last packet of a track is only written if it is NOT alone in the final
# fragment. Its duration is borrowed from the previous sample of the SAME fragment; when the queue holds
# a single packet at the final flush there is no such sample, the packet stays queued and is lost.
# Here the keyframe at pts 3 (100 ms) sets the split point; when the video packet pts 4 arrives the
# audio (last packet at 128 ms) has caught up, the first fragment is written with audio samples
# 0, 2048, 4096 (the audio packet 6144 is held back because it is the last one). At the final flush
# that audio packet is alone in its fragment, has no previous sample to borrow a duration from, and
# is silently lost, whereas the video track (two packets: pts 3 and 4) is written completely.
enc v video codec h264 width 320 height 240 fps 30/1 extra 000000016742c01ed900a047fe880000000168ce3c80
enc a audio codec aac rate 48000 extra 1190
mux mp4
pkt v 0 0 1 gen:10
pkt v 1 1 0 gen:10
pkt v 2 2 0 gen:10
pkt v 3 3 1 gen:10
pkt a 0 0 1 gen:10
pkt a 2048 2048 1 gen:10
pkt a 4096 4096 1 gen:10
pkt a 6144 6144 1 gen:10
pkt v 4 4 0 gen:10
finalise
dump
